# Dienogest + 10 DMF: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Analogous to Dienogest/DMSO/Dienogest_10DMSO_MD.inp.
#
# Starting geometry: Dienogest (48 atoms, from Dienogest_Opt_trj.xyz) + 10 DMF
#   molecules, each placed with its carbonyl O atom (the primary H-bond
#   acceptor site) on the same 12-direction sphere-shell pattern used
#   throughout this project, rotated so the molecule's bulk (the two methyl
#   groups) points radially outward.
#
# Dienogest centroid = (31.021, -20.109, -0.926); max atom-centroid distance
#   = 6.24 Ang.
# DMF's own extent from its O reference atom = 4.31 Ang (larger than DMSO's
#   3.78 Ang, since DMF's methyl groups reach further from the anchor atom).
# 10 DMF molecules placed at offset 10.0 Ang from Dienogest's centroid (same
#   offset used for the DMSO case).
# Cell Sphere radius set to 16.0 Ang (slightly larger than DMSO's 15.5 Ang,
#   to accommodate DMF's larger own extent).
# Checked: min DMF-Dienogest atom distance = 4.37 Ang (no clash), max atom
#   distance from the sphere center = 14.31 Ang (safely inside the 16.0 Ang
#   sphere). Total atom count = 168 (48 + 10x12), verified.
#
# NOTE: no SMD/CPCM here - this is a plain (unsolvated-continuum) XTB2 MD of
#   the explicit cluster, consistent with the other Explicit10 confined MD
#   runs in this project (XTB2 does not support SMD/CPCM in ORCA; continuum
#   solvation was never used for these confined MD pre-equilibration runs
#   anyway, only for the separate monomer/gas-phase reference calculations).

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.021, -20.109, -0.926, 16.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Dienogest_10DMF_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

